Changed: FE_RaviartThomasNodal now numbers the degrees of freedom on faces 2
and 3 of the reference cell in 3d with the z-coordinate running fastest, like
FE_Q and the face orientation tables. Before, the x-coordinate ran fastest,
and the normal component was not continuous across faces where face 2 or 3 of
one cell meets a face with a non-standard orientation, e.g., on the mesh of
GridGenerator::hyper_ball_balanced(). This changes the order of the degrees of
freedom of FE_RaviartThomasNodal in 3d. The new function
FE_RaviartThomasNodal::get_lexicographic_numbering() returns this numbering,
which MatrixFree now uses for this element.
<br>
